From: BerryMC <148406068+BerryMC@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:33:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Organize config files under a configs directory

Adopt the Sponge-style layout: bukkit.yml, spigot.yml, paper.yml,
commands.yml, help.yml and dionysus.yml all live under configs/ now.

- The jopt defaults for --bukkit-settings/--commands-settings/
  --spigot-settings/--paper-settings point into configs/, so admins
  can still override any file location via CLI flags.
- HelpYamlReader and DionysusConfig read their files from configs/.
- On startup, root-level files with the default names are MOVED into
  configs/ (one-time migration). Migration only runs when the matching
  CLI flag was not given and only when the target does not already
  exist, so custom layouts and CLI overrides are untouched.

server.properties, eula.txt, log4j2.xml and the JSON data files
(ops/whitelist/bans/usercache) stay at the root as before, and the
permissions.yml location remains configurable through bukkit.yml's
settings.permissions-file.

